render.mjs and the frame-by-frame contract (window.ready, renderAt, renderSheet, FRAME_ERRORS, shots, loops) come from
the painted-music-video skill's engine in this repository, which is based on ClaudeAnimationBase by John Heibel (MIT
licence, see LICENSE): https://github.com/JohnHeibel/ClaudeAnimationBase

Added for motion-film: any frame size and fps, DOM (screenshot) capture beside canvas capture, sub-frame motion blur,
onion skins, one-frame-per-beat sheets, the --inspect text checks, the --determinism check, sound-cue export for the
video-sound skill, machine-wide render slots, kit.js (closed-form springs, follow/edges/drag, cursor, typing, text
registry) and draw.js (flat motion-graphics helpers), and the looks in looks/.

